                        "sense_id": "f5e87f70-d375-3d2a-9b10-aae3e0bac0d3",
                        "entry_id": "6938fd5a-85ff-3be1-8053-dd30cb9fa749",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Helpless at birth (of young animals); or having young which are helpless at birth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "997552e8-20b7-41c5-8e0f-0faae6ee02f8",
                                "sense_id": "f5e87f70-d375-3d2a-9b10-aae3e0bac0d3",
                                "text": "Altricial young are typical among carnivores, which might be expected to be hampered in their hunting behaviour if the pregnant mother has to carry its young for a long period."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a74b534-60b5-4ba2-8a34-1e3dd399be05",
                                "sense_id": "f5e87f70-d375-3d2a-9b10-aae3e0bac0d3",
                                "text": "First, humans are altricial, with immature newborns and a long childhood."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd48cd1a-238a-4e22-83df-69fd2a01244e",
                                "sense_id": "f5e87f70-d375-3d2a-9b10-aae3e0bac0d3",
                                "text": "First, compared to other species, babies are altricial, meaning that they are weak, undermuscled, fat, and uncoordinated (sorry, babies, but it's true)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
